## Out of scope (deliberately deferred)

- **Issue #4 (Finished MAC)** — would derive two more keys
  (`data_c2s_finished`, `data_s2c_finished`) from `data_secret`
  using the same Expand pattern.  When issue-4 lands, add two
  more `MQC_HKDF_INFO_…_FINISHED` macros and two more Expand
  calls in `derive_data_keys`.  The plumbing is already in
  place after issue-3; the work is the Finished message itself,
  not the derivation.
- **Issue #5 (AEAD AAD)** — orthogonal; the derivation tree
  doesn't change.  Issue-5 only changes what bytes feed the
  AAD slot of `wc_AesGcmEncrypt` / `_Decrypt`.
- **Multi-stage TLS-1.3-style derivation tree** with separate
  `handshake_secret` → `master_secret` chaining via
  `Derive-Secret`.  Not needed for MQC since there is one input
  secret (no PSK, no early data); the single-Extract-with-full-
  transcript design above is sufficient.
- **Per-frame nonce randomness** beyond the per-connection IV
  (i.e., explicit nonce field on the wire).  Not justified —
  the IV-XOR-counter approach is the same one TLS 1.3 uses and
  is already best practice.
